// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch17 B07 side scene (optional): "The First Berth" (E, 4 min, ~180 words).
// act3_ch17.md §4. The dock-master breaks his silence, for Rhen, at the berth where Dace built his first boat here,
// TWENTY years ago (Ch15's ch15_two_daces has "twenty years ago trading salvage"; the sheet's "thirty" is superseded).
// The first words he has said since the night of the pyre-raft: two about Dace, the third about Tobin.
// If ch15_supper_with_father he starts more readily; if ch14_spoke_with_tobin Rhen can tell him Tobin's words.
title: ch17_first_berth
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@camera D12
@mark aldous_varrow first_berth walk
@mark rhen first_berth_b walk
<<if $ch15_supper_with_father>>
    @wait 2.0
<<else>>
    @wait 6.0
<<endif>>
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Your father built his first boat here. Badly. #line:ch17_berth_001
@wait 2.0
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [soft_smile]: Sang to the keel while he fitted it. As if it would listen. #line:ch17_berth_002
@anim aldous_varrow look_at mooring_post
@wait 3.0
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [sad]: Tobin used to sit on that post and tell him so. #line:ch17_berth_003
@wait 3.0
Rhen [tender]: He'd have told me too. #line:ch17_berth_004
<<if $ch14_spoke_with_tobin>>
    -> Tell him what Tobin said before the vows. #line:ch17_berth_005
        Rhen [tender]: Before the vows he told me nobody had to be chosen. He volunteered. Somebody had to go first. #line:ch17_berth_006
        @wait 3.0
        Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [grief]: That's him. Every word of it. #line:ch17_berth_007
        @wait 2.0
    -> Say nothing. #line:ch17_berth_008
        @wait 3.0
<<endif>>
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Your father's hull's in my last berth eleven years. I'd sooner it flew. #line:ch17_berth_009
@anim aldous_varrow hand_on rhen
@wait 2.0
<<set $ch17_first_berth = true>>
===
